uffers-10","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"Relación con TNet"},"704":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-11","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#buffers","content":"`Buffer` combina un flujo de memoria con las operaciones de `BinaryWriter` y `BinaryReader`. Es la pieza que Eco utiliza para construir, leer, copiar y reciclar datos binarios."},"705":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-12","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#escritura-y-lectura","content":"El ciclo básico es:"},"706":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-13","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#escritura-y-lectura","content":"El buffer controla internamente la posición y el tamaño útil de los datos."},"707":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-14","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#modos-del-buffer","content":"`BeginWriting` prepara el buffer para escribir y `EndWriting` finaliza esa fase. `BeginReading` cambia al modo de lectura y permite consumir los bytes existentes."},"708":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-15","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#modos-del-buffer","content":"Esto permite reutilizar la misma abstracción tanto para paquetes salientes como para datos recibidos."},"709":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-16","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"Las propiedades principales son:"},"710":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-17","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"Propiedad"},"711":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-18","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"Significado"},"712":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-19","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"`size`"},"713":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-20","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"Cantidad de datos útiles."},"714":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-21","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"`position`"},"715":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-22","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"Posición actual del flujo."},"716":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-23","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"`stream`"},"717":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-24","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"`MemoryStream` subyacente."},"718":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-25","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"`buffer`"},"719":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-26","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"Array interno que contiene la memoria."},"720":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-27","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"`isWriting`"},"721":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-28","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#tamaño-y-posición","content":"Indica si está en modo escritura."},"722":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-29","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#copia","content":"`CopyTo` permite copiar el contenido útil de un buffer a otro, evitando arrastrar espacio no utilizado del `MemoryStream`."},"723":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-30","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#reciclado","content":"Eco puede reutilizar buffers para reducir asignaciones. `Recycle()` devuelve el buffer al pool cuando el reciclado está habilitado."},"724":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-31","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#reciclado","content":"El código también incorpora comprobaciones de depuración para detectar usos incorrectos y dobles reciclados cuando las opciones correspondientes están habilitadas."},"725":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-32","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#seguridad-del-reciclado","content":"Un buffer reciclado no debe utilizarse posteriormente como si siguiera siendo válido. Las rutas de depuración de Eco permiten detectar esta clase de error."},"726":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-33","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#seguridad-del-reciclado","content":"Por eso las funciones que reciben un `Buffer` deben dejar claro quién posee su ciclo de vida."},"727":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-34","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#buffer-y-datagramas","content":"El mismo sistema de reciclado puede utilizarse con `Datagrama`, evitando crear memoria constantemente durante tráfico frecuente."},"728":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-35","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-paquetes","content":"Un `Paquete` define el significado de los bytes; un `Buffer` proporciona el espacio y las operaciones para escribirlos."},"729":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-36","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"`Buffer` es la evolución renombrada de `TNBuffer`. La arquitectura de pool, lectura/escritura y reciclado procede de TNet, mientras que la nomenclatura de Eco es la API utilizada por Pandora."},"730":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-37","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"Implementación del buffer binario."},"731":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-38","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"Repositorio upstream."},"732":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","type":"page","content":"Transporte","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Red","Red","Contenido","Transporte"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte"},"733":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-0","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","content":"Cómo Eco empaqueta, serializa y transporta datos entre clientes y servidor."},"734":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-1","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte#transporte","content":"Transporte"},"735":{"id":"/docs